{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1507535-paradox-and-the-supernatural-question","id":1507535,"title":"Paradox and the supernatural question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-05T19:37:40-07:00","id":1507535,"title":"Paradox and the supernatural question","content":"If a mage casts a spell against a supernatural creature is it considered vulgar with witnesses or it more dependent upon said creature's knowledge of mages and their abilities? I assume that if a Tremere is fighting a mage that he/she knows is a mage &amp; has a fireball thrown at him/her that it might have less paradox than if the vampire didn't know that they were fighting a mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24119-alucardtes","name":"Alucardtes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24119_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-05T19:43:45-07:00","id":1507537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucardtes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1507535-paradox-and-the-supernatural-question#post1507535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a mage casts a spell against a supernatural creature is it considered vulgar with witnesses or it more dependent upon said creature's knowledge of mages and their abilities? I assume that if a Tremere is fighting a mage that he/she knows is a mage &amp; has a fireball thrown at him/her that it might have less paradox than if the vampire didn't know that they were fighting a mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it depends on the creature in question, if it's clearly a supernatural creature it would be easier and it doesn't rationalize the situation, if it still looks like a human being then I think it won't make that much difference. A tremere for being technically dead is not part of humanity, at least that's what I believe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-05T19:54:18-07:00","id":1507539,"title":"","content":"There was an old Magazine called Inquest (I think it was affiliated with Wizard magazine, it certainly resembled Wizard in more than a few ways) that was one of my biggest sources on old WoD (before early 2000s at least). They said Vulgar magic around other Supernaturals is <i>still</i> Vulgar magic, albeit without mortal witnesses. Their last words on the subject: &quot;Even around Werewolves, change into a wolf too often and you may end up one for <i>real</i>, and that means no more spheres.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-05T20:02:41-07:00","id":1507540,"title":"","content":"Inquest Magazine was the renamed &quot;White Wolf Magazine&quot;. It was awesome!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-05T20:05:32-07:00","id":1507541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alqamar Alaswad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1507535-paradox-and-the-supernatural-question?p=1507540#post1507540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Inquest Magazine was the renamed &quot;White Wolf Magazine&quot;. It was awesome!</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. Strange, I remember they said only <i>one</i> of the editors was much of an expert on White Wolf (actually it was more like they said &quot;he might be a real vampire&quot;).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-05T20:11:29-07:00","id":1507544,"title":"","content":"Paradox at work, maybe? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-05T23:08:20-07:00","id":1507555,"title":"","content":"Nightfolk (aka what Mage20 terms any non-Awakened supernatural) do not count as witnesses by default. Non-humans in general don't count as Sleepers either. The implication is that to call extra attention from reality to make Paradox worse an actual witness has to have a soul capable of Awakening. It's the nascent spark within humanity to become mages that makes them &quot;special&quot; in this regard. It's possible that some supernatural beings, especially ones dependent on a specific Reality Zone to exist at all, might align so much with the rules of that Reality Zone that they could count as witnesses against magic that violates the rules of it; even some mages can be that way, and the game refers to anything in that state as Sleepwalker to impart the idea that they're in between the Awakened and Sleepers.<br /> <br /> This is covered in the books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-06T03:05:05-07:00","id":1507569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1507535-paradox-and-the-supernatural-question?p=1507555#post1507555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nightfolk (aka what Mage20 terms any non-Awakened supernatural) do not count as witnesses by default. Non-humans in general don't count as Sleepers either. The implication is that to call extra attention from reality to make Paradox worse an actual witness has to have a soul capable of Awakening. It's the nascent spark within humanity to become mages that makes them &quot;special&quot; in this regard. It's possible that some supernatural beings, especially ones dependent on a specific Reality Zone to exist at all, might align so much with the rules of that Reality Zone that they could count as witnesses against magic that violates the rules of it; even some mages can be that way, and the game refers to anything in that state as Sleepwalker to impart the idea that they're in between the Awakened and Sleepers.<br /> <br /> This is covered in the books.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This imply that gilguled mage don't count as witness either","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-06T03:58:51-07:00","id":1507572,"title":"","content":"Yes, though they'd not count anyway because they'd still have the beliefs from being a mage previously that would make them not Sleepers like acolytes/etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-06T04:19:53-07:00","id":1507575,"title":"","content":"Agreed. Once you have Awakened, there's no going back to Sleep. That said, being gilguled takes you out of that spectrum entirely, as they have about as much influence over reality as a rock does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-06T06:34:13-07:00","id":1507578,"title":"","content":"Even among sleepers, not everyone counts as a witness. Only those whose beliefs largely conform to the local consensus do. Someone who grew up in a Traditions Horizon Realm will not function as a Witness in New York City, nor will a New Yorker function as a witness in many Horizon Realms. Likewise, someone from the stone age would not count as a modern witness, although a Geico caveman probably would.<br /> <br /> So while Werewolves and Changelings might not count as witnesses because they don't have sleeper souls, Kinfolk, Ghouls, and arguably Vampires* don't count as Witnesses because their day to day life experience is so vastly different from the Consensus. The distinction is largely academic in a standard setting, but as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> said, it might matter in a setting where one of the Night Folk was culturally dominant.<br /> <br /> *Vampires have a shredded or damaged Avatar, not a completely different soul. That's why they are incapable of Awakened magic, but it is unclear if it changes their potential impact on the Consensus.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-06T10:46:04-07:00","id":1507590,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure that interaction between Reality Zones and Sleepers is correct. Humans raised in highly specialized Reality Zones like a Horizon Realm are very likely not Sleepers any more anyway (either being Sleepwalkers, acolytes, or cultists by that point). By the books a full Sleeper is a Sleeper regardless of Zone, and being in wildly different Reality Zones makes them more likely to be witnesses because they're not going to be as easily thrown off by things like Mythic Threads that wouldn't apply to their original Reality Zone.<br /> <br /> What you're talking about is more in line with the concept of Sleepwalkers where enough buy-in to specific belief systems makes someone's status as a Sleeper more contextual without them going all the way to being awake even if not Awakened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-06T12:44:45-07:00","id":1507596,"title":"","content":"Yes, a sleeper is a sleeper regardless of zone, but that doesn't mean they count as witnesses. A citizen of the Roman Republic transported to today wouldn't be able to tell the difference between a coincidental Hypertech, vulgar Hypertech, and a desk lamp. They'd all seem vulgar to him, but only one of them would actually violate the local Consensus. We're left with three possibilities:<br /> <br /> 1) He doesn't count as a witness at all.<br /> 2) He counts as a witness only when his idea of vulgar overlaps with the Consensus' idea of vulgar.<br /> 3) He counts as a witness for any magical effect that he would find impossible.<br /> <br /> The third option is bad form because it makes something Vulgar With Witnesses in his presence and Coincidental outside of it, and for a variety of reasons I think that's a bad idea. The other two are workable though my preference is for the first. Our hypothetical Roman is simply not close enough to the Hypothetical Bystander to act as a stand in.<br /> <br /> For what it is worth M20 does make the distinction between Sleeper and Witness. It's on page 531 and in typical M20 fashion it clearly defines something (&quot;a Sleeper witness is someone whose beliefs conform to the local ideas about what is and is not possible.\u200b&quot;) and then muddies the waters by giving contradictory explanations of what that means. Overall you could read any of the above three possibilities out of it, though I think the second is likely the most charitable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":".  Because the forum somehow converts \u201c#2\u201d to Onyx Path 04-06-2023, 09:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-06T19:30:18-07:00","id":1507639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1507535-paradox-and-the-supernatural-question?p=1507596#post1507596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, a sleeper is a sleeper regardless of zone, but that doesn't mean they count as witnesses.</div> </div> </div> </div>If they don't qualify for another title (since the game has more than Sleeper and Awakened for the options here), then yes, they do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A citizen of the Roman Republic transported to today wouldn't be able to tell the difference between a coincidental Hypertech, vulgar Hypertech, and a desk lamp. They'd all seem vulgar to him, but only one of them would actually violate the local Consensus. We're left with three possibilities: </div> </div> </div>Here's a much simpler way of addressing it: anyone put through that drastic of a shift would automatically become a Sleepwalker. Problem solved, no complex metaphysical considerations. This also means you don't have to deal with the fact that the Roman lived at a time where Paradox literally worked differently.<br /> <br /> Sleeperwalkers are already a thing. We have a game-term for people that should be conditional/situational in their witness status to separate them from normal Sleepers that just default count as witnesses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The third option is bad form because it makes something Vulgar With Witnesses in his presence and Coincidental outside of it,... </div> </div> </div>This doesn't actually follow based on your phrasing of the options. If the effect is coincidental within the Reality Zone, the presence of someone that would count as a witness in other Reality Zones doesn't make it Vulgar, so their witness status is irrelevant.<br /> <br /> If a completely normal modern person goes into a Hermetic Sanctum, the Hermetic's magic that is only coincidental because it's in a Sanctum stays so.<br /> <br /> Large scale Reality Zones are not dictated by one person. Your hypothetical Roman doesn't override the Reality Zone. They can only mess with things like Mythic Threads and Blatancy because those require manipulating the situation to avoid scrutiny from onlookers and account for people not buying it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-06T22:13:14-07:00","id":1507655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucardtes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1507535-paradox-and-the-supernatural-question#post1507535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a mage casts a spell against a supernatural creature is it considered vulgar with witnesses or it more dependent upon said creature's knowledge of mages and their abilities? I assume that if a Tremere is fighting a mage that he/she knows is a mage &amp; has a fireball thrown at him/her that it might have less paradox than if the vampire didn't know that they were fighting a mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I recall, Vampires and Garou ( and other Nightfolk, Magical Beings, and Supernatural Persons ) do not cause problems or disruptions in regard to casting Magick Effects regardless of their knowledge. attitude, emotions, or actions.<br /> This comes distinctly with being who they are in regard to their particular powers, aura, capabilities, and qualities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-06T23:31:54-07:00","id":1507663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1507535-paradox-and-the-supernatural-question?p=1507639#post1507639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This doesn't actually follow based on your phrasing of the options. If the effect is coincidental within the Reality Zone, the presence of someone that would count as a witness in other Reality Zones doesn't make it Vulgar, so their witness status is irrelevant.</div> </div> </div> </div>The closest that the game comes to addressing the issue of witnesses to Coincidental effects is the optional Domino Effect rule, which could kind of be interpreted as a sort of \u201cCoincidental with Witnesses\u201d situation; though I personally view it more as a borderline-Vulgar effect: it's still <i>technically</i> Coincidental, but \u201caffect[s] the scene in noticable ways: exploding gas mains, unlikely ricochets, unexpected appearances of the police\u2026 that sort of thing.\u201d Which sounds about awful lot like \u201cVulgar\u201d to me; so much so that my own house rule replacement for Domino Effect is to say that starting with the third time that a \u201cwild coincidence\u201d takes place in a scene, it becomes Vulgar.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> It's not <i>quite</i> \u201cCoincidental with Witnesses\u201d, because it doesn't actually require there to <i>be </i>any Witnesses; only that the Coincidence be unlikely enough that a Hypothetical Observer would balk at it happening repeatedly. But with the Domino Effect in play, there <i>is</i> a distinction made between two types of Coincidental Effects: those that are subject to the Domino Effect, and those that aren't.<br /> <br /> \u2026which is a bit of a tangent, because it doesn't actually contradict your point that the presence of absence of Witnesses doesn't have an effect on Coincidental Effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 04-07-2023, 02:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-07T08:29:32-07:00","id":1507690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1507535-paradox-and-the-supernatural-question?p=1507639#post1507639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This doesn't actually follow based on your phrasing of the options. If the effect is coincidental within the Reality Zone, the presence of someone that would count as a witness in other Reality Zones doesn't make it Vulgar, so their witness status is irrelevant.<br /> <br /> If a completely normal modern person goes into a Hermetic Sanctum, the Hermetic's magic that is only coincidental because it's in a Sanctum stays so.<br /> <br /> Large scale Reality Zones are not dictated by one person. Your hypothetical Roman doesn't override the Reality Zone. They can only mess with things like Mythic Threads and Blatancy because those require manipulating the situation to avoid scrutiny from onlookers and account for people not buying it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's pretty much a restatement of what I was saying so I think we are largely in agreement other than word choice. While I can see the merit in specific terms, there are so many Sleeper categories that do not function as witnesses (acolytes, enlightened citizens, cultists, hunters, members of extremely isolated cultures, etc) that a generalized distinction is easier.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Here's a much simpler way of addressing it: anyone put through that drastic of a shift would automatically become a Sleepwalker. Problem solved, no complex metaphysical considerations. This also means you don't have to deal with the fact that the Roman lived at a time where Paradox literally worked differently.<br /> <br /> Sleeperwalkers are already a thing. We have a game-term for people that should be conditional/situational in their witness status to separate them from normal Sleepers that just default count as witnesses. </div> </div> </div>Here I disagree. Sleepwalker is already carrying too much weight. It is used for Sleepers who are quite magically aware (hedge wizards, for instance), but it also encompasses people who are halfway awake and Mages who are in denial. While neither of those count as witnesses, they also don't count as Sleepers.<br /> <br /> It's not that Sleepwalker can't also encompass consensus outsiders, but the term is already a metaphysical mishmash so it doesn't make the issue easier to talk about. A more specific term would be better. That or just saying &quot;A witness is a sleeper whose beliefs conform with the local consensus of what is and isn't possible&quot; which is something Mage already gives us.<br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-07T16:51:25-07:00","id":1507718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1507535-paradox-and-the-supernatural-question?p=1507690#post1507690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's pretty much a restatement of what I was saying so I think we are largely in agreement other than word choice.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm confused. You said point 3 would result in turning coincidental effects into vulgar effects. I pointed out why that wouldn't happen. That's a bit more than a word-choice nit-pick.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While I can see the merit in specific terms, there are so many Sleeper categories that do not function as witnesses (acolytes, enlightened citizens, cultists, hunters, members of extremely isolated cultures, etc) that a generalized distinction is easier. </div> </div> </div>1) M20 uses the word &quot;assistant&quot; to be the game-term that encompasses the in-game terms like acolyte, enlightened citizen, etc.<br /> 2) Hunters and isolated cultures are not, by default, non-witnesses. Hunters have to belong to a category that grants them that status independent of trying to kill magic-users. Isolated cultures are examples of what creates small pockets of Reality Zones in modern times, and the people in them are still normal Sleepers, just ones in a Reality Zone.<br /> <br /> You're making this way more complicated than it is. Yes, we are dealing with some overlapping categories that's more like a Venn Diagram than some hard exclusive definitional categories... but Mage tends to do that a lot because of it's inherent flexibility.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sleepwalker is already carrying too much weight. It is used for Sleepers who are quite magically aware (hedge wizards, for instance), but it also encompasses people who are halfway awake and Mages who are in denial. While neither of those count as witnesses, they also don't count as Sleepers. </div> </div> </div>i don't see the case here. A Sleepwalker is someone who's status isn't clean cut between witness or non-witness. Sleepwalking mages <b>do</b> count as witnesses depending on the circumstances; at it's worse case they can count as a witness against their own magic.<br /> <br /> Again, it feels like you're overdoing this by trying to create hard line distinctions instead of treating things like &quot;Sleepwalker&quot; as a modifier that adjusts the basic rules for those it applies to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-08T02:50:15-07:00","id":1507752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1507535-paradox-and-the-supernatural-question?p=1507690#post1507690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's pretty much a restatement of what I was saying so I think we are largely in agreement other than word choice. While I can see the merit in specific terms, there are so many Sleeper categories that do not function as witnesses (acolytes, enlightened citizens, cultists, hunters, members of extremely isolated cultures, etc) that a generalized distinction is easier.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>In many countries, regions, and areas it would be easier to consider the categories and groups who do not count as witnesses for Magick Effects ; rather than to identify the few groups who are witnesses disruptive to Magick Effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 04-09-2023, 02:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-08T11:33:23-07:00","id":1507772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1507535-paradox-and-the-supernatural-question?p=1507752#post1507752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In many countries, regions, and areas it would be easier to count and consider the few categories and groups who count as witnesses for Magick Effects, rather than count who disrupts them by being nearby.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure what distinction you're trying to make between \u201ccount as witnesses\u201d vs. \u201cdisrupts them by being nearby\u201d. \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-08T23:51:26-07:00","id":1507840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1507535-paradox-and-the-supernatural-question?p=1507772#post1507772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure what distinction you're trying to make between \u201ccount as witnesses\u201d vs. \u201cdisrupts them by being nearby\u201d. \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for the comment, I corrected the post so that it is hopefully clear and understandable.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-09T00:27:28-07:00","id":1507843,"title":"","content":"What areas/etc. are you thinking of that wouldn't just classify as a Reality Zone hostile to different magic than standard Consensus?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-09T00:58:17-07:00","id":1507844,"title":"","content":"That was my thought, too. The thing about Reality Zones is that, almost by definition, the majority of the local Sleepers will count as Witnesses to what the Zone defines as Vulgar. \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-10T05:31:27-07:00","id":1507934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1507535-paradox-and-the-supernatural-question?p=1507718#post1507718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm confused. You said point 3 would result in turning coincidental effects into vulgar effects. I pointed out why that wouldn't happen. That's a bit more than a word-choice nit-pick.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, that was my reason for rejecting option 3. You said it wouldn't work that way and gave an explanation that basically made options 2 and 3 identical. Since we both rejected the consequences of option 3, it seems we are largely in agreement.<br /> <br /> The main difference seems to be whether we say the Roman Out of Time is not a Witness, or we say he is a Witness but that only matters when, by happenstance, he overlaps with the consensus. That's largely a matter of word choice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1507535-paradox-and-the-supernatural-question?p=1507718#post1507718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) M20 uses the word &quot;assistant&quot; to be the game-term that encompasses the in-game terms like acolyte, enlightened citizen, etc.<br /> 2) Hunters and isolated cultures are not, by default, non-witnesses. Hunters have to belong to a category that grants them that status independent of trying to kill magic-users. Isolated cultures are examples of what creates small pockets of Reality Zones in modern times, and the people in them are still normal Sleepers, just ones in a Reality Zone.</div> </div> </div> </div>The isolated cultures thing is on me. That was supposed to mean someone from an isolated culture who is outside of their reality zone. It's a distinction Mage makes, and one that I made in the Roman example, but did not specify in the list.<br /> <br /> With that correction, the list I gave were all people that M20 said either did not count as witnesses, or only situationally counted as witnesses. Including hunters.<br /> <br /> For the record I agree with you about the hunters. Which group of hunters the list is referring to doesn't change anything about my point, though.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1507535-paradox-and-the-supernatural-question?p=1507718#post1507718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're making this way more complicated than it is. Yes, we are dealing with some overlapping categories that's more like a Venn Diagram than some hard exclusive definitional categories... but Mage tends to do that a lot because of it's inherent flexibility.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know where you are getting the idea that I want hard line distinctions. I wonder if that's why it looks like we are on opposing sides when we are advocating for similar things. I like your idea for using something like Sleepwalker as a modifier that adjusts the rules. I just think that Sleepwalker has too much baggage to be that term.<br /> <br /> I also think there's no reason to reach that far. There is a term. We've been given it. It's Witness. We even have an easy definition of who does and does not count as one. As easy as Mage gets anyways.<br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-10T15:34:40-07:00","id":1507966,"title":"","content":"&quot;Sleepwalker&quot; isn't really caring that much weight when you look at what it does rather than try to mix in and out of game thoughts on it. The whole point of all the terms we're discussing is &quot;who counts as a witness, and when of that's in question,&quot; so that's not really a functional word to use as it would just create a circular loop.<br /> <br /> But really this isn't complicated. There are three groups divided by two binaries. Are they Awakened, and is their default status as a witness to vulgar magic.<br /> <br /> Sleepers (N, Y).<br /> Nightfolk (N, N)<br /> Mages (Y, N)<br /> <br /> Then we have two modifier groups that both result in the same key point: they are exceptions to the default statuses according to their base grouping. The big difference is that Assistants are actively aware of, and involved in Awakened society on some level, letting them aid magic despite not being Awakened, while Sleepwalkers are generally unaware of their situational status as it comes from deeply internalized beliefs that can easily go unexamined.<br /> <br /> You keep saying that we're arguing for the same thing, but it feels like we're not because of things like &quot;Sleeperwalker carries too much weight,&quot; even though your example is the exact sort of thing it was thought up to encompass. You keep trying to add more groups (even if they're just in-character names for the same thing), and it feels like you're just trying to muddy the waters around things that just aren't that hard. Hedge wizards, for example, are Nightfolk (unawakened, not witnesses), but have a much higher rate of being Assistants than other Nightfolk, and much higher rates of being Sleepwalkers if trained exclusively by Mages and other hedge wizards associated with those same mages (esp. the Technocracy).<br /> <br /> So we might be advocating for similar things, but I strongly feel like I'm arguing that this is way simpler and easier to grok that it can seem once you take the in-character stuff out of the equation, and you seem to be advocating that we have to account for all the in-character labels that are acknowledged by the books as not being 100% accurate to how the world of Mage actually is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-10T16:11:50-07:00","id":1507975,"title":"","content":"I'm used to \u201cNight Folk\u201d being a term that means \u201cthe other playable supernatural types\u201d: vampires, werewolves, wraiths, and changelings; and if using the End Nights plots, Imbued, mummies, demons, and projectors. While I personally would put sorcerers under that label as well, that's just me; mortals who have access to supernatural powers typically <i>aren't </i>classed as Night Folk, even if the powers they access are the ones that are otherwise exclusive to Night Folk (e.g., ghouls, kinfolk, mediums, and kinain). <br /> <br /> The technical definition of Sleepwalker in M20, which I quoted earlier in this thread, essentially covers the (N, N) category you mentioned at the start of your last post: they're people who aren't Awakened, but who don't count as Witnesses. The definition even strongly implies that they probably have access to supernatural powers of their own (specifically, anything that <i>isn't</i> Sphere Magick); but that's technically phrased as something that's optional.<br /> <br /> So you have Sleepers (N/Y), Sleepwalkers (N/N), and Awakened (Y/N). <br /> <br /> To the extent that there's mud in the waters, it's that there are Sleepers who don't <i>always</i> count as Witnesses, such as members of a Cult. These Sleepers are the ones you're calling Assistants; and they're basically individuals who are straddling the line between Sleeper and Sleepwalker. I tend to think of them as \u201cSleepers who have developed a Focus\u201d: like the Awakened, they have a solid philosophy about how the world actually works, which manifests as a Paradigm, Practice, and Instruments \u2014 though in there case, the latter two only matter in terms of what approaches of Magick they're suited to support: they can't use Magick themselves. If they observe Magick that's compatible with their Focus, they don't count as Witnesses; if they encounter Vulgar Magick that <i>isn't </i>compatible with their Focus, they do. <i>\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b</i>\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-10T16:19:21-07:00","id":1507976,"title":"","content":"The book uses the term assistants: M20. p. 532 (and other places, but that's where it defines Ally vs. Assistant vs. Cultist).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-10T18:06:18-07:00","id":1507983,"title":"","content":"Fair enough; and in particular, it uses it as an umbrella term for Extraordinary Citizens and Acolytes: Extraordinary Citizens are Technocratic Assistants, while Acolytes are the Traditions' Assistants. They, <i>and</i> Cultists (who are described as being like assistants, but with even more dedication), are the ones I was talking about in the last paragraph of my previous post: the Sleepers who nonetheless don't count as Witnesses to <i>your</i> Magick, even if they count as Witnesses to others' Magick.<br /> <br /> And for what it's worth: where I disagree with M20 is that it portrays the matter of Assistants in terms of science vs. magic: Extraordinary Citizens don't count as Witnesses for Hypertech, but <i>do </i>count as Witnesses for all kinds of non-hypertech (so far, so good); but Acolytes don't count as Witnesses for <i>any</i> Magick: the book emphasizes that you'd need to come from a remote and isolated corner of the globe not to buy into hypertech, and implicitly assumed that Assistants either accept or reject <i>every kind of</i> mysticism the same way. The implication is that there's no such thing as an acolyte that buys into<i> one</i> style of mysticism but rejects <i>others</i>.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, that may be a Traditions-specific thing, going along with that group's focus on ecumenical mysticism. Disparate Assistants (whatever they're called) might be a bit more like Extraordinary Citizens in that they don't count as Witnesses to their own Craft's Magick, but <i>do</i> count as Witnesses to Magick that clashes with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 04-10-2023, 09:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-11T04:47:47-07:00","id":1508016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1507535-paradox-and-the-supernatural-question?p=1507966#post1507966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You keep saying that we're arguing for the same thing, but it feels like we're not because of things like &quot;Sleeperwalker carries too much weight,&quot; even though your example is the exact sort of thing it was thought up to encompass.</div> </div> </div> </div>I keep saying we are arguing for similar things and our differences are mostly of word choice. That we disagree on the use of 'Sleepwalker' is very much word choice.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1507535-paradox-and-the-supernatural-question?p=1507966#post1507966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So we might be advocating for similar things, but I strongly feel like I'm arguing that this is way simpler and easier to grok that it can seem once you take the in-character stuff out of the equation, and you seem to be advocating that we have to account for all the in-character labels that are acknowledged by the books as not being 100% accurate to how the world of Mage actually is.</div> </div> </div> </div>It probably is simpler from your point of view. From my point of view you are overcomplicating things and I'm advocating for a very simple underlying principle. Yet I do think we are still trying to say broadly the same thing about who does and does not count as a witness, we're largely in agreement about why they do, we just don't agree on the best way to explain it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1507535-paradox-and-the-supernatural-question?p=1507983#post1507983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And for what it's worth: where I disagree with M20 is that it portrays the matter of Assistants in terms of science vs. magic: Extraordinary Citizens don't count as Witnesses for Hypertech, but <i>do </i>count as Witnesses for all kinds of non-hypertech (so far, so good); but Acolytes don't count as Witnesses for <i>any</i> Magick: the book emphasizes that you'd need to come from a remote and isolated corner of the globe not to buy into hypertech, and implicitly assumed that Assistants either accept or reject <i>every kind of</i> mysticism the same way. The implication is that there's no such thing as an acolyte that buys into<i> one</i> style of mysticism but rejects <i>others</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was exactly what I was referring to when I said earlier that M20 muddied the waters. It comes across very much like a section that was written for convenience rather than because it matched an underlying truth of the game. Nothing is specifically wrong with it, but it strongly seems like there should be people who fall in the intervening space. By the same token, people who have &quot;totally escaped the influence of modern technology&quot; as M20 put it would not just reject Technomagic, they'd reject quite a bit of Traditions magic as well.<br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-11T05:44:11-07:00","id":1508021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1507535-paradox-and-the-supernatural-question?p=1508016#post1508016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That we disagree on the use of 'Sleepwalker' is very much word choice.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>But your case is an entirely subjective appeal to it &quot;carrying too much,&quot; when all it effectively means is that a character's status as a witness is variable. It's carrying one concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}